      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-02-08_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <head>BLACK DRESSES.</head>
        <p>BLACK DRESSES.</p>
        <p>As in previous Bale 3 there will be several piles of black Dress Lnigths thrown out at mix,cl prices 6s. lid es. 9d., 10s. 6d,, 12s. 3d., and is. 9d. The goods are the remains of our regular stock and are reduced from is. 6d. is. 11d., 2s. 6d. ands. 6d. per yard. 2000 yds. of the finest all-wool black French Cashmere 461 n. wide at is. 71d. per yd. or 93...91. per 6 yds., instead of 2s. lid. per yd. The stock ol black wool. mohair and silk Crepons is limited to about 530 yds. These will be sold at about Half-price irrespective of cost. 75 pieces of vari: us:makes in plain Serges, plain Cloths, and fancy all-wool black materials will be much reduced to make room for Spring delivery.</p>
        <p>f DRESS SKIRTS. About 93 colored and black Dress Skirts from ;As Ild cto 21s. Some of these area quarter what they cost. Real Aberdeen and Perth Skirt lengths reduced to 4s 6d. 5s 6d, and 6s 11d. 4000 yards of various Washing Materials for Dresses. All one price, 4a per yard. Most ot these are Hail-price. SILK DEPARTMENT. • Upwards of £7OO worth of Silks for this safe. The demand for Silks and Satins during the last season both for morning and evening wear has necessitated a very large increase of stock. , , As far as possible these will be divided into lots.. Lot I—Rich i Satins in every colons, gold, pink, white, creme, pale blue, &amp;c , to be sold at is. 9d. per yd. during the sale. 'These satins have never been ret-dled under 2s. 11d, Lot 2—All shot Suralis will be sold is, lid, per yd. instead of 2s 41d., 2s, 6d., and 2s. lid. Lot 3—All coloured Bengalines marked 2s. lid. and 3s. tel.. usual prices 3s. 11d. and ss. 6oi. ,Lot 4—Odd lengths of Canton Pongees and other siLks at Hid per yard. Lot 5-250 yards Embossed Silk for Blouses or Dresses 90. usual price ls Lot 6—Special lot of about 350 yards pure Silk Surah in tar- tans for ladies' blouses will be so.d at Is. 9d. per yard. These goods are very fashionable and ard worth 2s. lid.</p>
        <p>11.1ANTLE DEPARTMENT. . All Goods in this Department are this Season's purchase. •</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-02-08_WidnesExaminer_art0006" n="art0006">
        <head>LADIES' JACKETS.</head>
        <p>LADIES' JACKETS.</p>
        <p>About 60 stylish Black Curl and Brown Cloth Jackets, newest shapes, from 8s lid to 425. 35 Ladies' Coloured Cloth Jackets. from 15s 6d to 39s 6d, some very hao dsorne for trimmed jackets included. 45 Maids' and young Ladies' Jackets, great bargains. Some exceptional bargains in Ladies' Summer Jackets and Capes, masked down at nominal prices to clear. 27 Ladies' Costumes (coat and skirt), high class goods, 10e 6d to 425. This lot are neatly half-price. About 120 Ladies' Black and Coloured Capes. This lot in- chides all our handsome pattern mantles. The whole to be sold at nearly half-price. Upwards of 75 Ladies' Mackintoshes and Waterproofs, all tke newest goods, irom 8s 6,1 to 37s 6d.</p>
        <p>FUR DEPARTMENT. A magnificent collection of High-class Furs, all of the Choicest Skins. Upwards of 250 Stoles. Necklets, Boas, Victoriae, etc., to be cleared (these are an exceptional lot). 37 Muffs, in sable, bear, otter, beaver, skunk, etc. Special Bargains.</p>
