        <p>Cotrnillor ROBERTS moved the confirmation oK the minutes,and alluding to the conferences with counsel io London: with regard to certain slight alterations proposed to be made in the agreements,said that acting upon the advice Gf counsel they were about to make suggestions which were fair and reasonable,and which they hoped to get adopted in principle. seeing, that they did not entrench upon anything which the Ship Canal Company</p>
