        <p>GR",2ALKING pRIIOT, c 1 ity anything, a grand mimic, age four years, will lend on approval. Price £l2;or would exchange for first class up-to-date PNEUMA- TIC BICYCLE 1?y good maker.—MESSENGER, 52. St. James'- at., Liverpool.</p>
        <p>ORRTTY POLLY ! Yes, the •• Parrot Trick " has been woiited saccessfully many a time and oft. Your safest plan, is to go to some large importer and purchase direct from him. Of course it is his aim to supply good birds, as each one is an advertisement. Remember his address re- mains the same, while the swindler changes his repeatedly.— Copied from the 'Yorkshire Weekly Post., ' —WILLIAM Caoss, 'Liverpool. the Largest Importer of Birds, Beast., and Reptiles in the World. 800 Cages.</p>
        <p>SORE SHOULDERS, SORE BACKS, Scc., quickly CURED BY CONDY'S FLUID. Veterinary Book free from .61, Turnmill-Street, E. C. Horses suffering from wounds, cuts, nruiqes, troken knees, 4sackEd heels, grease or thrush. CURED in a few hours by bathing the parts affected with Condy's Fluid. ._4iluted). It makes the hair grow where rubbed off. Prices, '8 et. is.: 20 oz., 2s. of all Chemists. VETERINARY BOOK free containing full directions for , curing, dis.ases lf Horses, Dogs, Lc. from CoNDY's 'Wm]) WoRK.S. 61. Turnmili-street.London.E .C.</p>
        <p>MACKENZIE'S FEMALE REMEDY. One case guaranteed to remove the most OBSTINATE OBaTRUCTICNS and IRREGULARITIES in 12 hours HARMLESS. Nothing can re:ist it. Failure is impossible Bead stamped envelope tor PARTICULARS. TESTI. IKONIALS. and ADVICE. Ours is the most POWERFUL and STRONGEST Remedy Sold, and in no single cas,. has it ever failed—even in the wait longstanding, intricate, pud lingering cases. Post free, under cover, with written guarantee of cure ss. (five shillings).—Mrs. W. E. MACKENZIE', Trafford House. 83. Dawes-road. Fulham, Loudon. Mention paper</p>
        <p>. , THE DEAF HEAR. Deafness, Head Nois and all other distressing ailments ' es, associated with lose of hearing. absolutely cured by using AURALINE ESSENCE" after all else has failed. Itils most marvellous medical discovery of the Nineteenth Century. •Acts like a charm. Hundreds of grateful testimonials. Sufferers ! Why remain deaf when a cure awaits von? Post free, 2s. 9d. per Bottle. THE MACKEY REMEDY COMPANY, HA. High Holborn. London.--Beware of injuri- ous instruments and other appliances.</p>
        <p>H. EZARD, BUILDER AND CONTRACTOR, FEARNHEAD, WARRINGTON. Estimates given for Alterations and Repairs of every description (Town and Country). Hous.s.built to tenants own plans. Jobbing puPctually attended to. Rent and Fire and Life Assurance Agent.</p>
        <p>T" " MULTUM IN PARVO "FARMERS' ACCOUNT BOOK is still to the front of all others; 35., with Pocket Wage Book.—WF.LLS, Hatfield, Doncaster.</p>
        <p>BOON TO LADIES, COLLINS' MARVELLOUS FEMALE REMEDY. Mr. COLLINS (who was :30 years a member of the Royal College of Suroeons of England) will f9rward. Free of Charge full PARTICULARS of a REMEDY which, during an exten- sive practice both at home and in the Colonies, he has never know to fail in the most OBSTINII.TE CASES OF OBSTRUC- TION and IRREGULARITIES. Send addressed envelope for full particulars, and waste no more time and money on useless Pills and so-called Remedies, ac., which, the majority df cases, are nothing but PURGATIVES, and cause SICK ESS, PROSTRATION, and PAIN, without having the desired effect. Letters to be addressed D. COLLINS, Gothic House, 9, Erskine-street. Llverposl.</p>
        <p>SUPERIOR SECON.D-HAND FURNITURE, by all the noted and very best makers, removed from halls, man- sions, hotels, offices, private houses of every description, and which undergo a thorough examination and ate placed in condition equal to new. I may here remark that the stock I offer is considerably larger thßn at any other house in the city, and is not being placed in the market because it is soiled or damaged in any menner ; but am pleased to state that in cousequence of the great increase in my trade, and the large number of orders I have to deliver every week, I find it ab- solutely necessary and therefore deelded to make extensive alterations which willincur an outlay of some hundreds of pounds. And have arranged with the contractors to clear the showrooms previous to the workmen commencing opera- tions, and in order to do so I have decided to give my cus- tomers the benefit of the enormous reductions rather than store the stock, which embraces furniture of every descrip- tion; in fact, such an assortment of bedroom suites, dining. room suiLes, drawing-room suites, office furniture, bookcases. desks, sideboards, dinner waggons. cabinets, overmantels, davenports, card, work and fancy tables, carpets, rugs, bed- steads, bedding, fender, pianos, and every article for com- pletely furnishing the mansion or cottage. Can nowhere be seen except at GERSHON'S Universal Furnishing Arcade, 44, Oldham-st, In fact, when the alterations are completed. which will consist of</p>
        <p>NEW OFFICES, NEW COUNTING HOUSE, NEW DINING SALOON for the employee,</p>
        <p>NEW REFRESHMENT-ROOM for convenience of customers NEW CARPET SALOON, NEW SHOWROOMS;</p>
        <p>And other internal Alterations, all local and outside shops will sink to insignificance.</p>
        <p>THB following will convey but a faint idea of the Mar- vellous Bargains on v.ew, any of which may be stored free of charge till required. TERMS (4? BUSINBSS DURING THE SAL%</p>
        <p>GOODS EXCHANGED IF NOT SATISFACTORY.</p>
        <p>EXPERIENCED MEN SENT TO FIX AND FIT UP. GOODS PACKED AND DELIVERED FREE. CARPETS MADE FREE.</p>
        <p>LOCK-UP STORE ROOMS FOR CONVENIENCE OF CUSTOMERS.</p>
        <p>And, lastly, if you purchase on my Deferred Payment System I Charge a Simple Five per Cent Extia. Every customer attended to by a member of the firm, which prevents the annoyance of a salesman who charges high prices in order to make a big commission. Bankers—Manchester Joint-Stock Bank. Telegrams—" Universal," Manchester.</p>
        <p>DURING the Sale, Magnificent Solid Oak DINING- ROOM SUITE, comprising a grand couch, two noble easy chairs, and six superior spoon-back chairs,all in splendid condition, not soiled; originally cost £55, sale price 9gs. Grand Sideboard to match, Tgs., worth £4O; Dining Table to match, 635. In addition to above, we have a truly magnificent Col- lection of Dining-room Suites, over 200, with Sideboards, Dining Tables, and Overmantels to match. An inspection will prove the fact that nowhere can such an assortment be seen except at GERSHON'S, the Universal Furnishing Arcade, 44, Oldham-street, next to the Adelphi Bank, Man- chester. Note.—The above may be had on my deferred payment syste-n for a simple five per cent extra added to invoice. SPECIAL ATTENTION to Lot 166, which is in Pollard Oak and without a doubt the best and handsomest IGt in Manchester. The Sideboard, which is 7a. long and very lofty, can only be described as simply magnificent and the most unique in design we have ever seen. The Suite of 12 small chairs (may be had with a less number), two large Lounge Chairs, and large Couch, are all stuffed with hair and covered in morocco leather, guaranteed. The Dining-table, on carved supports, is very hsndsome, having a number of loose leaves. We offer the lot for 145 gs. ; cost over £4OO. We may state that sgs. each will be allowed for any of the small chairs not required. We wish to irapress upon the public that every lot advertised is on our premises and hundreds of others. Remember address, GERSHON'S Old-established Universal Furnishing Arcade, 44, Oldham-street (next to the Adelphi Bank), Manchester. Note.—lf on the deferred payment system only five per cent. extra added to invoice.</p>
        <p>LOT 237 is in Oriental Saddle Bags, carved walnut frames. consisting of half-dozen small chairs, two er.sv chairs, and couch ; trice £25, reduced for the sale to .22 1 -., Side- board to-match, with bevelled-glass back, a p -1..... • .tity ; sale price, £6 155., usual price 12gs. Dining ' 68s. 6d. Three other Suites in Saddle Bags, real Persia", - erlasting ware, splendid patterns, among which is a wat,r lily, most charming and pleasing; the wood work in -these suites is American walaut, brown oak, and mahogany. and the prices are 18, 25, and 36gs. ; they each cost £lO, £l5, and £25 a suite more. Sideboards. Tables, and Overmantels to match, all on view in our showrooms. Hundreds of other Suites on view. Call and inspect for yourselves; you will not be un- duly pressed to buy. We have no salesmen or walking gen- tlemen who work for a commission. Every customer is attended to by a member of the firm at GERSHON'S Univer- sal Furnishing Arcade, 44, Oldham-street (next to Adelphi Bank), Manchester. Note.—lf on the deferred payment system only five per cent. extra added to invoice.</p>
        <p>I OT 97 is a Charming DINING-ROOM SUITE, in embossed IA leather, very handsome and stylish, frame work beauti- fully carved; the six stendard chairs have padded backs, the two easy chairs are large arid comfortable, and the couch is most luxuriously upholstered. This suite is in solid American walnutwood and is suitab'e for high-class dining-room. Usual price, 251„5. ; sale price. 15gs. A Another Suite, in Solid Mahogany, in good hard grain leather. Crornwellian style ; sound in every respect; not soiled. Recently been recovered. A marvel of cheapness; only 9gs. Another in Walnut, covered in leather, reduced to sgs. Sideboard, to match, 423. ; table, 21s. These bargains are on offer during the sale and before alterations are commenced. Inspection invited.</p>
        <p>SWEEPING 'SEDUCTIONS. MUST CLEAR PREVIOUS TO ALTERATIONS. LOT 51 is a BEDROOM SUITE. Those wishing to furnish a bedroom in high-class style and good taste should Inspect it, for style, workmanship, and design it cannot be equalled, the massive large size wardrobe with two bevelled glass doors of rare brilliancy reaching from plinth to cornice; the full-size pedestal dressing table, double washstand to match, pedestal bedside cupboard, towel airer, and three chairs, the whole are in rosewood. richly inlaid with tulip, box, olive, and other rare woods. The cost of this noble Suite was £lOO. bale price 55gs. Another Suite in • walnut cost £125 for 60gs , and another in Spanish mahogany cost £55 for 27gs. Special attention is requested to Lots 6,7, 8 and 9, which are Suites in walnut, silver birch, mahogany, and ash, each Suite hasa large wardrobe, with Levelled glass door: dressing table with large b -yelled glass attached, supported by carved bracket's restingon raised jewel drawers; it also forms a chest of drawers, being enclosed by four drawers; the large wash stand is also enclosed, and has a marble slab, tile back, and bevelled shaving glass above, towel rail, pedestal bedside cupboard, and three chairs. These suite a: e guaranteed solid, no veneer being used. Sale price, 151 gs. Other suites smaller from 24 153. Inspection Invited. Any of the abov may be stored free of charge t''' required.</p>
        <p>GERSHON'S NOTED UNIVERSAL FURNISHING ARCADE, 44, OLDHAM-STREET (Next to Adelphi 'Bank), MANCHESTER. Note.—lf on the deferred payment system only 5 per cent. extra added to invoice.</p>
        <p>MUST CLEAR for the Contractors. Such a chance seldom occurs.</p>
        <p>STUP FINDOUS BARGAINS</p>
        <p>We now enter the Miscellaneous Department. Hera we can inspect a splendid assortment of second-hand hair-seated Furniture. A first class solid mahogany sofa 50s„ cost per- haps £6 ; another less in size 38s. Spanish Mahogany couch. in hair seating, 475.; ditto 635.. cost £6. Very fine solid Spanish mahogany sofa, very heavy and massive, bean re- upholsterel, cost when new £B. for four guineas. Others in American leather from 16s. Now we see over 50 pairs of easy chairs in stock. Several gents' easy chairs at 15s. each. mahogany easy chair, in hair, for 285.. cost 60s. Superior pair of Cromwell easy chairs, large and massive, cost £B, for four guineas the pair. Nothing better can be made, Lady's rocking chair, in hair, 28s. A. very large quantity ol hal:- seated chairs from ss. each to 245. each. An enormous stock of kitchen furniture is here displayed at marvellously low prices. For an instance, strong kitchen chairs 2s. each,kitchen tables from 6s. 6d. each; grand Spanish mahogany, dresser, with high carved back, cost £l4, for 6 guineas ; another, cost £ll.for 5 guineas; painted dresser, with thick top, 285.; another, very handsome high back. 60€.; and others at a" prices at</p>
