        <p>LY,IIII V. LADTMA.RN.-At Lvmrn. F3r the first ten minuteg Lvmm ore-zed hat could not score. The visi- tors then atf•acked but were repulsed. After a good run and contra bv Dinnin-r, James 14,,ah scored for Lymm • The visitors pressd. and one of the Lymm backs headed through his own goal. in the second half Fogg scored for Lvmm, and the game ended—Lymm, two goals; Ladybarn, one.</p>
